<title>UK: Cable &amp; Wireless mulls Panama move - paper.</title>
<headline>Cable &amp; Wireless mulls Panama move - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cable &amp; Wireless Plc (C&amp;W) is considering a multi-million dollar bid for a 49 percent stake in Panama's state-controlled telecoms business Intel, Britain's Sunday Telegraph newspaper reported.</p>
<p>It said C&amp;W would be competing for the stake in Intel, said to be worth some $2 billion in total, with GTE Corp of the United States.</p>
<p>The paper said C&amp;W would have to decide in the next few weeks whether to make a bid. It said the stake would complement C&amp;W's other activities in the area, such as its presence in 15 Caribbean countries.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
